demás, el hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos en diciembre no implica que se haya actuado de forma irregular.\nQué se puede revisar: Es necesario comprobar si los contratos adjudicados en diciembre están relacionados con la misma necesidad. También se debe revisar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos por necesidad funcional o por otras razones. Otra comprobación sería analizar si los contratos están distribuidos de forma equilibrada entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 31 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 0.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 77.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 19.7 to 668.3. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 3% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 17 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,800 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the limit does not mean that any of them were improperly awarded. It could reflect normal market pricing, budget constraints, or the need for multiple smaller contracts to meet specific requirements.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what services were provided and the dates of delivery. Also, review the contracts to see if multiple contracts were used for the same purpose, which could indicate a need for separate agreements. Look for patterns in the timing of awards to determine if there's a consistent schedule or random distribution.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["cc4DgEUyYgtVYjgxA4nMUw%3D%3D","dHpyfUKKe7YeIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D","PI6G3ElI3IPyoM4us5k4vw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}